course: dictionary
lesson: 7758
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Puppy» usually means a young dog, but it also appears in phrases such as «puppy fat» and «puppy love». Context tells you which meaning the writer means.
explain: Look at the words around the tricky word. «A puppy is a young dog, so "no dogs allowed" includes puppies.» The sentence gives the meaning straight away: a puppy is a young dog.
explain: Now test a phrase. In «puppy fat», the word puppy does not mean a dog at all. Try the dog meaning in the sentence: "soft young dog fat" makes no sense, so the phrase has its own meaning, soft fat that goes away as children grow.
fact: A puppy is a young dog. More than one puppy is puppies.
fact: «Puppy fat» is soft fat some children have that goes away as they grow.
fact: «Puppy love» is a young person's first, sweet love.
fact: Puppies need their vaccinations before walking where other dogs go, because serious illnesses spread through dog poo and spit.
fact: A microchip about the size of a grain of rice can be put under a puppy's skin at the vet's.
exercise: «A puppy is a young dog, so "no dogs allowed" includes puppies.» What is a puppy? | A kind of cat | *A young dog | A grown-up dog with a very long tail | A large bird
exercise: Lucy says, «Her puppy fat is going as she gets taller.» What does puppy fat mean? | A fluffy coat on a young dog | Fat that a dog gets from eating too much | *Soft fat some children have that goes away as they grow
exercise: In «a litter of puppies», what is the plural of puppy? | *puppies | puppys | puppy's | puppie
test: Sam had puppy love for his friend Ana, so he always smiled when she came in. What does puppy love mean here? | *A young person's first, sweet love | A love for pets only | A love of puppy food | A love of dog shows
test: «Puppies need their vaccinations before walking where other dogs go.» Why do they need them? | *Serious illnesses spread through dog poo and spit | Puppies are too heavy to carry | Dogs don't like walks | Vaccinations make puppies grow faster
exam: Bella reads, «A microchip about the size of a grain of rice slides under the skin between a puppy's shoulder blades.» Which meaning of puppy is used? | Puppy love | *A young dog | Puppy fat
